677a695,727
>      * Prefer the line that most recently *successfully* asserted
>      * (ica_interrupt_cpu got past the gate and called host_set_hw_int).
>      * This honours temporal order across raise/intack and closes a race
>      * window where, on WHP, another thread can set a higher-priority IRR
>      * bit between our raise and the CPU thread's intack -- which would
>      * otherwise let priority scan pick the racing IRQ and starve the
>      * one we actually meant to deliver.
>      *
>      * Only used if the remembered line is still pending in IRR (i.e.
>      * the raise hasn't been clobbered by a clear_int) and not masked
>      * out by IMR and not blocked by a higher-priority bit in ISR.
>      * Otherwise we fall through to the standard scan -- so command.com
>      * etc. (no race) get identical behaviour to before.
>      */
> #if defined(HAXM)   /* HAXM/WHP builds only (WHP = HAXM && HYPERV); CCPU excluded */
